      <data key="d17">The current housing market lacks affordable, energy-efficient single-family homes that meet modern sustainability standards while providing comfortable living spaces for growing families</data>
      <data key="d18">Estimated total project cost: $425,000 (including land acquisition, materials, labor, permits, and contingencies)</data>
      <data key="d19">Expected ROI: 15-20% upon completion and sale, with potential for higher returns if held as rental property. Energy savings provide ongoing operational ROI of 8-10% annually</data>
      <data key="d20">Alternative 1: Standard construction - lower upfront cost but higher operating expenses
Alternative 2: Luxury construction - higher quality but significantly higher budget
Alternative 3: Modular/prefab construction - faster timeline but limited customization
Selected approach balances quality, sustainability, and budget constraints</data>
      <data key="d21">Proceed with the energy-efficient residential construction project as it aligns with market demand, sustainability goals, and provides competitive financial returns while establishing our company as a leader in green building practices</data>
